1
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:08,010
Next tool, metal fab laser, welder, 1200 watt unboxing and first use.

2
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:10,090
Take out all the items.

3
00:00:10,090 --> 00:00:12,470
Pay attention to the unboxing tips.

4
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:14,450
Open the lid first.

5
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:48,650
Pull apart from the side to open and remove the enclosure.

6
00:00:48,650 --> 00:00:58,140
Take out the welding head first, then remove the foam.

7
00:00:58,140 --> 00:01:27,700
Wind the cable on the side of the main unit, and place the welding head on the bracket.

8
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:30,220
Place the main unit.

9
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:34,900
Leave a gap of more than 10 centimeters at the front and back of the main unit.

10
00:01:34,900 --> 00:01:44,140
Lock the four caster wheels.

11
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:54,270
Connect the shielding gas cylinder.

12
00:01:54,270 --> 00:02:01,330
Insert one end of the tube into the shielding gas inlet on the main unit.

13
00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:05,690
Connect the other end of the tube to the cylinder, or gas generator.

14
00:02:05,690 --> 00:02:13,260
Place the welding head.

15
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:34,260
Assemble the welding head cradle.

16
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:36,360
Place the welding head on the cradle.

17
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:44,120
Connect the workpiece sensing cable.

18
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:48,080
Insert the connector end into the port for the workpiece sensing cable.

19
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:52,390
Connect to a power supply.

20
00:02:52,390 --> 00:02:58,710
This product requires a 220 to 240 volt AC power supply, and works at a rated power of

21
00:02:58,710 --> 00:03:03,470
4.2 kilowatts and a full load current of 21 amperes.

22
00:03:03,470 --> 00:03:08,670
An individual branch circuit with a current carrying capacity of 25 amperes or above is

23
00:03:08,670 --> 00:03:09,670
recommended.

24
00:03:09,670 --> 00:03:12,790
Ensure that the power supply is grounded.

25
00:03:12,790 --> 00:03:16,030
The connection of power cables varies with their standards.

26
00:03:16,030 --> 00:03:23,750
If hard wiring operation is required, it should be performed by a professional electrician.

27
00:03:23,750 --> 00:03:27,070
Attach the round connector of the power cable to the main unit.

28
00:03:27,070 --> 00:03:34,940
The larger pin faces upward.

29
00:03:34,940 --> 00:03:40,000
Check the emergency stop button.

30
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,720
Ensure that the emergency stop button is released.

31
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:47,700
Insert the key.

32
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:50,760
Insert the key into its designated port.

33
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:53,720
Power on and unlock the device.

34
00:03:53,720 --> 00:04:03,640
On the back panel of the main unit, turn on the power switch to activate the device.

35
00:04:03,640 --> 00:04:08,490
On the touchscreen, select a language and unit.

36
00:04:08,490 --> 00:04:13,190
The first time you turn on the device, you will see a QR code on the touchscreen.

37
00:04:13,190 --> 00:04:18,310
Scan the QR code to watch the safety training videos.

38
00:04:18,310 --> 00:04:23,090
After watching the video, input the serial number shown on the touchscreen to the web.

39
00:04:23,090 --> 00:04:26,210
To generate an unlock password for your device.

40
00:04:26,210 --> 00:04:29,970
On the touchscreen of your device, tap enter the password.

41
00:04:29,970 --> 00:04:34,390
Enter the password generated to unlock your device.

42
00:04:34,390 --> 00:04:36,670
Calibrate the focus for the welding head.

43
00:04:36,670 --> 00:04:41,070
On the home page of the touchscreen, tap system settings and check the value of focus

44
00:04:41,070 --> 00:04:45,420
scale reference.

45
00:04:45,420 --> 00:04:48,280
Check if the graduated tube is of the same value.

46
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:50,700
If yes, no calibration is needed.

47
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:53,440
If not, adjust the graduated tube.

48
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:54,820
Open the fastener.

49
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:58,860
Push or pull the graduated tube to adjust it to the reference value.

50
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:01,060
Connect the wire feeder.

51
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:05,380
The wire feeder is used to feed wire in laser welding, and it is not needed in metal

52
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:06,900
cleaning or cutting.

53
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:09,860
Place the wire feeder on the left side of the main unit.

54
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:12,860
Lock the four caster wheels.

55
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:14,460
Connect to the main unit.

56
00:05:14,460 --> 00:05:17,420
Use the wire feeder cable to connect them.

57
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:22,460
The small protrusion on the inner wall faces upwards.

58
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:24,340
Insert the connector.

59
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:30,100
Screw the metal part.

60
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:31,580
Install the drive rolls.

61
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:37,860
This video exemplifies installing 1mm welding wire on the 1mm guiding rail.

62
00:05:37,860 --> 00:05:40,540
Open the wire feeder.

63
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:44,620
Open the wire feeding driver.

64
00:05:44,620 --> 00:05:49,400
Remove the screws.

65
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:53,770
Install the drive rolls.

66
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:57,550
Install the screws back.

67
00:05:57,550 --> 00:06:06,940
Store the other pair of drive rolls above the wire feeding driver.

68
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:09,580
Install the wire feeding tube.

69
00:06:09,580 --> 00:06:12,180
Close the right tensioner.

70
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:16,580
Loosen the screw on the right side of the wire feeding driver.

71
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:20,700
Insert the end of the wire feeding tube without a fastener to the wire feeder.

72
00:06:20,700 --> 00:06:24,580
Slide the nozzle in until its stem presses against the right panel of the wire feeding

73
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:25,940
driver.

74
00:06:25,940 --> 00:06:28,140
Tighten the screw to fix the nozzle.

75
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:30,020
Open the right tensioner.

76
00:06:30,020 --> 00:06:35,460
Load the welding wire.

77
00:06:35,460 --> 00:06:40,540
Unscrew the cap and remove the sleeve.

78
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:49,090
Align the hole with the pin.

79
00:06:49,090 --> 00:06:52,730
Ensure that the wire spool is installed in the correct direction.

80
00:06:52,730 --> 00:06:56,970
After released, the wire comes out from the bottom of the wire spool to enter the wire

81
00:06:56,970 --> 00:06:58,650
feeding driver.

82
00:06:58,650 --> 00:07:04,890
Install the sleeve and the cap back.

83
00:07:04,890 --> 00:07:06,330
Take out the wire end.

84
00:07:06,330 --> 00:07:11,870
Do not release the wire or it will unravel.

85
00:07:11,870 --> 00:07:15,830
Cut off the bent end of the wire.

86
00:07:15,830 --> 00:07:21,060
Thread the wire into the wire feeding driver.

87
00:07:21,060 --> 00:07:23,740
Press the wire slightly to make it pass through.

88
00:07:23,740 --> 00:07:31,340
Ensure that the wire passes through the drive rolls into the wire feeding tube.

89
00:07:31,340 --> 00:07:34,700
Close the tensioners.

90
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:43,930
Rotate the tensioner's knobs to adjust the wire feed tension.

91
00:07:43,930 --> 00:07:47,970
Feed the welding wire.

92
00:07:47,970 --> 00:07:54,290
When delivered, the wire feeding tube is installed with a 0.8 slash 1.0 nozzle at the end with

93
00:07:54,290 --> 00:07:57,950
a fastener.

94
00:07:57,950 --> 00:08:00,390
Press and hold the feed button on the wire feeder.

95
00:08:00,390 --> 00:08:04,310
The wire spool rotates counterclockwise at a constant speed.

96
00:08:04,310 --> 00:08:07,670
When the wire extends from the nozzle, stop wire feeding.

97
00:08:07,670 --> 00:08:13,270
If the wire extends too far, press the retract button to return the wire.

98
00:08:13,270 --> 00:08:16,710
Close the door of the wire feeder.

99
00:08:16,710 --> 00:08:20,190
Install the wire feeding tube on the welding head.

100
00:08:20,190 --> 00:08:21,630
Open the fastener.

101
00:08:21,630 --> 00:08:23,870
Slide it onto the welding head tip.

102
00:08:23,870 --> 00:08:27,710
Ensure that the wire comes out from the groove of the welding nozzle.

103
00:08:27,710 --> 00:08:33,570
Close the fastener.

104
00:08:33,570 --> 00:08:39,020
Fine tune the wire.

105
00:08:39,020 --> 00:08:42,300
Secure the wire feeding tube.

106
00:08:42,300 --> 00:08:44,860
Place back on the welding head cradle.

107
00:08:44,860 --> 00:08:48,860
Use X-Tool Metal Fab Laser Welder 1200 watts.

108
00:08:48,860 --> 00:08:54,020
Before operating the device, please follow the safety instructions to put on PPE and

109
00:08:54,020 --> 00:08:56,740
take proper safety precautions.

110
00:08:56,740 --> 00:09:02,740
Necessary PPE includes laser safety goggles, welding helmets, dust mask, laser and heat

111
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:05,980
resistant gloves, clothing and aprons.

112
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:09,930
Ensure that the workroom is well ventilated.

113
00:09:09,930 --> 00:09:12,570
Laser welding in standard mode.

114
00:09:12,570 --> 00:09:18,610
Ensure that a gas flow meter is fitted to the gas cylinder or gas generator.

115
00:09:18,610 --> 00:09:22,560
Ensure that enable lasering is off.

116
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:26,300
Open the gas cylinder valve.

117
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:30,380
Press and hold the grip sensing button and trigger to allow gas flow.

118
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:37,410
Meanwhile, adjust the gas flow rate to 15 to 30 liters per minute.

119
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:40,510
Press the workpiece on a metal base.

120
00:09:40,510 --> 00:09:45,010
Clamp the workpiece sensing cable to the workpiece or to a conductive object connected with the

121
00:09:45,010 --> 00:09:46,010
workpiece.

122
00:09:46,010 --> 00:09:50,930
It is strictly prohibited to attach the clamp to the graduated tube of the welding head.

123
00:09:50,930 --> 00:09:54,850
Press the feed and retract buttons on the welding head to adjust the wire until its

124
00:09:54,850 --> 00:09:57,730
tip coincides with the red spot.

125
00:09:57,730 --> 00:10:01,010
Calibrate the welding head if the red spot falls at the left or right side of the

126
00:10:01,010 --> 00:10:05,130
extended wire or if the spot is not visible or blurred.

127
00:10:05,130 --> 00:10:09,330
Refer to the calibrate the red spot position part in maintenance.

128
00:10:09,330 --> 00:10:14,250
Turn on the wire feeding enable switch to enable the auto feeding function.

129
00:10:14,250 --> 00:10:17,930
On the touch screen, choose standard mode, weld.

130
00:10:17,930 --> 00:10:21,850
Select the material type, material thickness and wire diameter.

131
00:10:21,850 --> 00:10:25,050
Tap enable wire feeding to allow wire feeding.

132
00:10:25,050 --> 00:10:28,210
And tap enable lasering to allow laser emission.

133
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:29,610
Align the parts to be welded.

134
00:10:29,610 --> 00:10:34,010
Aiming the welding nozzle at the starting point, press and hold the grip sensing button

135
00:10:34,010 --> 00:10:36,930
and trigger to start welding.

136
00:10:36,930 --> 00:10:41,030
Tack weld the starting and ending points first, then start seam welding.

137
00:10:41,030 --> 00:10:45,530
As the welding head feeds the wire forward, a reaction force is generated from the welding

138
00:10:45,530 --> 00:10:48,750
point that pushes the welding head backward.

139
00:10:48,750 --> 00:10:52,190
Simply hold the welding head steady and guide the direction.

140
00:10:52,190 --> 00:10:56,230
To avoid wire sticking, do not press the welding head downward.

141
00:10:56,230 --> 00:11:00,170
After the welding is completed, the workpiece and parts of the welding head will remain

142
00:11:00,170 --> 00:11:01,170
hot.

143
00:11:01,170 --> 00:11:04,050
Do not touch the hot areas without protection.

144
00:11:04,050 --> 00:11:07,770
Turn off enable wire feeding and enable lasering.

145
00:11:07,770 --> 00:11:10,090
Laser cleaning.

146
00:11:10,090 --> 00:11:12,090
Turn off the device.

147
00:11:12,090 --> 00:11:16,780
Remove the wire feeding tube.

148
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:18,940
Remove the welding nozzle.

149
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:22,660
Replace with the cleaning nozzle.

150
00:11:22,660 --> 00:11:24,900
Turn on the device.

151
00:11:24,900 --> 00:11:26,000
Tap clean.

152
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,620
Tap enable lasering.

153
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:28,620
Tap confirm.

154
00:11:28,620 --> 00:11:32,580
Aim the cleaning nozzle at the starting point with the welding head parallel to the

155
00:11:32,580 --> 00:11:34,240
weld seam.

156
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:44,880
Press and hold the grip sensing button and trigger to start laser cleaning.

157
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:47,380
Laser cleaning is completed.

158
00:11:47,380 --> 00:11:49,440
Laser cutting.

159
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:54,600
On the touch screen, tap system settings and take down the value of focus scale reference.

160
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:56,720
Turn off the device.

161
00:11:56,720 --> 00:12:02,460
Open the fastener to remove the current tip.

162
00:12:02,460 --> 00:12:05,660
Insert the cutting tip.

163
00:12:05,660 --> 00:12:08,860
Keep consistent with focus scale reference.

164
00:12:08,860 --> 00:12:10,740
Close the fastener.

165
00:12:10,740 --> 00:12:14,940
Place the gas flow meter on the cylinder with a gas pressure reducing valve.

166
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:20,020
Turn on the device and check if the welding head emits a clear and integral red spot.

167
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:25,780
If not, calibrate the red spot position to avoid burning the nozzle during laser cutting.

168
00:12:25,780 --> 00:12:33,480
Adjust the air pressure to 0.8 to 1.2 MPa.

169
00:12:33,480 --> 00:12:34,480
Tap cut.

170
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:37,320
Select the material type and material thickness.

171
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:38,880
Tap enable lasering.

172
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:40,160
Tap confirm.

173
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:44,680
Start laser cutting.

174
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:46,800
Laser cutting is completed.

175
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:48,760
Replace the wire feeding nozzle.

176
00:12:48,760 --> 00:12:52,920
The wire feeding tube has an end with a fastener and a replaceable nozzle.

177
00:12:52,920 --> 00:13:02,770
You need to replace the nozzle based on the diameter of the welding wire.

178
00:13:02,770 --> 00:13:05,650
Next tool, MetalFab CNC cutter.

179
00:13:05,650 --> 00:13:08,210
Unboxing and first use.

180
00:13:08,210 --> 00:13:13,510
Unbox the package following the instructions on it.

181
00:13:13,510 --> 00:13:17,590
Leave a clearance of at least 1 meter around the package before unboxing.

182
00:13:17,590 --> 00:13:24,860
First, release the seven latches on the front panel.

183
00:13:24,860 --> 00:13:28,620
Lay down the panel as a ram.

184
00:13:28,620 --> 00:13:33,300
Then release the three latches on the left panel.

185
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:36,460
Release the three latches on the right panel.

186
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:40,340
And release the three latches on the rear panel.

187
00:13:40,340 --> 00:14:29,230
At last, remove all the other panels except the bottom one.

188
00:14:29,230 --> 00:14:32,550
Tear open the black strap securing the main unit.

189
00:14:32,550 --> 00:14:37,180
Remove the plastic bag.

190
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:40,460
Lift the four leveling feet.

191
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:43,260
Use the wrench to loosen the top nuts clockwise.

192
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:49,640
Manually turn the top nuts until they touch the lower nuts.

193
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:53,240
Use the wrench to loosen the lower nuts counterclockwise.

194
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:56,440
Manually turn the leveling feet counterclockwise to lift them.

195
00:14:56,440 --> 00:15:01,160
The leveling feet should be about 1 centimeter above the limit blocks.

196
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:09,660
Move the machine down the ramp.

197
00:15:09,660 --> 00:15:13,590
Move the machine to the desired position.

198
00:15:13,590 --> 00:15:18,520
Leave at least 50 centimeters around the machine for assembly.

199
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:21,440
Lower the leveling feet to secure the machine.

200
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:25,960
Manually turn the leveling feet clockwise to lower them until they touch the ground.

201
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:29,200
Use the wrench to tighten the lower nuts clockwise.

202
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:33,880
Manually turn the top nuts counterclockwise until they touch the main unit base plate.

203
00:15:33,880 --> 00:15:38,380
Then use the wrench to secure them.

204
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:40,740
Lift the main unit.

205
00:15:40,740 --> 00:15:44,380
Remove the four fixing bars at the bottom corners.

206
00:15:44,380 --> 00:15:47,620
Use the hex key to loosen the screws.

207
00:15:47,620 --> 00:16:00,010
Remove four fixing bars.

208
00:16:00,010 --> 00:16:02,410
Lift the main unit following the instruction.

209
00:16:02,410 --> 00:16:12,460
At the back of the main unit, use the Z-shaped wrench to lift the main unit.

210
00:16:12,620 --> 00:16:16,020
Meanwhile, pay attention to the white lines on the side.

211
00:16:16,020 --> 00:16:19,380
Get at eye level with the base beam to observe the white line.

212
00:16:19,380 --> 00:16:28,510
When the white line is level with the base beam, stop lifting the main unit.

213
00:16:28,510 --> 00:16:31,790
Install four long fixing bars.

214
00:16:31,790 --> 00:16:35,430
Align the holes on the long fixing bar to those of the main unit.

215
00:16:35,430 --> 00:16:41,500
Screw in four screws to secure the bar.

216
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:43,940
Install the other three bars in the same way.

217
00:16:43,940 --> 00:16:49,100
Then use the hex key to fully tighten all the screws on the four bars.

218
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:52,660
Install four short fixing bars.

219
00:16:52,660 --> 00:16:57,660
The four bars shall be attached to the front, left, and right sides of the machine.

220
00:16:57,660 --> 00:17:00,140
Mind the installation direction of the bars.

221
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:14,200
Align the holes and secure the bars with screws.

222
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:18,080
Install the side plates.

223
00:17:18,080 --> 00:17:21,880
Align the grooves in the side plate with the protrusions on the main unit.

224
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:28,560
Push the side plate towards the main unit.

225
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:34,690
Secure the side plate with two screws.

226
00:17:34,690 --> 00:17:36,650
Install the front plate.

227
00:17:36,650 --> 00:17:40,290
Align the protrusions on the front plate with the grooves in the main unit.

228
00:17:40,290 --> 00:17:43,370
Push the front plate towards the main unit.

229
00:17:43,370 --> 00:17:56,120
Secure the front plate with four screws.

230
00:17:56,120 --> 00:17:58,640
The front plate is installed.

231
00:17:58,640 --> 00:18:02,200
Install the back plate.

232
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:05,760
Align the grooves in the back plate with the protrusions on the main unit.

233
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:08,160
Push the back plate towards the main unit.

234
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:21,430
Secure the back plate with five screws.

235
00:18:21,430 --> 00:18:24,270
The back plate is installed.

236
00:18:24,270 --> 00:18:26,510
Install the base plate.

237
00:18:26,510 --> 00:18:33,930
Align the base plate with the slots and push it in.

238
00:18:33,930 --> 00:18:37,930
To prevent the base plate from deformation due to prolonged processing,

239
00:18:37,930 --> 00:18:42,650
please add an appropriate amount of sand or water into the base plate for heat insulation.

240
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:56,250
Install the exhaust fan. Ensure that the side with arrows is facing up.

241
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:05,640
Attach the connector of the exhaust fan to that of the main unit.

242
00:19:08,090 --> 00:19:11,290
Tuck the excess connecting wire into the hole of the exhaust fan.

243
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:17,120
Align to the four pins on the main unit and install the fan.

244
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:23,120
Gently press the fan down to make it fully seated.

245
00:19:29,900 --> 00:19:32,780
Slide the clamp onto the pipe. Fit to the fan.

246
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:38,760
Tighten the pipe clamp clockwise to secure the smoke exhaust pipe.

247
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:43,280
Slide the pipe clamp onto the exhaust pipe.

248
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:46,880
Insert the pipe connector to the pipe.

249
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:51,840
Tighten the pipe clamp clockwise to secure the connection.

250
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:58,720
Snap the pipe connector to the corresponding port of X-Tool Safety Pro AP2 Max.

251
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:05,920
For more information on how to use AP2 Max, refer to its quick start guide and safety instructions.

252
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:14,460
Install other accessories. Align the external antenna with the hole at the back of the main unit.

253
00:20:14,460 --> 00:20:27,740
Tighten the antenna clockwise. Lift the antenna upwards. Align the holes of the hook with those

254
00:20:27,740 --> 00:20:42,480
of the machine. Secure the hook with screws. Install the welding head. Insert one end of

255
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:52,800
the communication cable to the EX-Control port at the back of the machine. Then rotate the

256
00:20:52,800 --> 00:21:01,790
connector clockwise to tighten it. Insert the other end to the X-Control port of X-Tool Metal

257
00:21:01,790 --> 00:21:07,390
Fab Laser Welder. Then rotate the connector clockwise to tighten it. Open the protective

258
00:21:07,390 --> 00:21:12,430
lid of the machine. Three wing bolts are pre-installed in the machine. Please take

259
00:21:12,430 --> 00:21:17,390
them out before use. Loosen the bolts counterclockwise and take out the bolts in the tabs.

260
00:21:22,060 --> 00:21:28,620
Take out the welding head from X-Tool Metal Fab Laser Welder. Open the fastener. Remove the welding tip.

261
00:21:30,680 --> 00:21:33,960
Align the protrusion on the cutting tip with the slot in the welding head.

262
00:21:34,920 --> 00:21:42,860
Insert the cutting tip. Close the fastener. Straighten the cable with the welding head

263
00:21:42,860 --> 00:21:49,900
firmly held. Loop the welding head cable around the back of the carriage. Align the two grooves

264
00:21:49,900 --> 00:21:59,580
on the side of the welding head with the two fixing pins of the carriage. Close the toggle latch.

265
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:17,050
Secure the three fixing rings on the cable to the corresponding slots. Snap the cable into the

266
00:22:17,050 --> 00:22:22,170
clamp. Ensure that the cable is fixed in place and doesn't touch the X-axis guide rail.

267
00:22:22,890 --> 00:22:34,890
Install the cable fixing block. Before use, connect X-Tool Metal Fab CNC cutter to a power supply.

268
00:22:35,050 --> 00:22:42,330
Connect X-Tool Metal Fab Laser Welder to the power supply. Push the connector into the power

269
00:22:42,330 --> 00:22:48,490
port of X-Tool Metal Fab Laser Welder. Rotate to secure the power cable. Connect the other end of

270
00:22:48,490 --> 00:22:53,130
the power cable to a circuit that meets requirements. Wiring operations should be

271
00:22:53,130 --> 00:22:58,490
performed by a professional electrician. For more details, see X-Tool Metal Fab

272
00:22:58,490 --> 00:23:03,770
Laser Welder's Quick Start Guide. Ensure that the emergency stop buttons of the two machines

273
00:23:03,770 --> 00:23:18,030
are released. Insert the key into its designated port of X-Tool Metal Fab Laser Welder. Shielding

274
00:23:18,030 --> 00:23:24,110
gas inlet. Remove the dustproof cap. Insert one end of the tube into the shielding gas inlet.

275
00:23:24,110 --> 00:23:30,030
Connect the other end to the gas cylinder or air compressor and air dryer. Then open the valve

276
00:23:30,030 --> 00:23:41,070
according to the instructions for the cylinder or devices. Press the power switch. Press the power

277
00:23:41,070 --> 00:23:50,030
switch. Download XCS. Download the latest version of XCS at X-Tool official website.

278
00:23:55,150 --> 00:24:02,190
Connect your X-Tool Metal Fab CNC cutter in XCS. Ready to go through the three calibration tasks.

279
00:24:02,190 --> 00:24:11,150
Calibration Task 1. Active vibration compensation. Click Start. Read the tips and click Start.

280
00:24:16,730 --> 00:24:21,530
Read the tips in the dialog box. Press the start slash stop button on the machine.

281
00:24:31,600 --> 00:24:38,320
Click Done after the active vibration compensation concludes. Calibration Task 2. Laser focus

282
00:24:38,320 --> 00:24:47,960
calibration. Click Start. Read the tips in the dialog box. Click Next. Follow the tips in XCS

283
00:24:47,960 --> 00:24:54,510
to adjust the cutting tip. Turn off the two machines. Take out the welding head.

284
00:24:54,510 --> 00:25:05,720
Open the fastener. Pull out the cutting tip slowly. Use the 2.5 millimeter hex key included

285
00:25:05,720 --> 00:25:12,240
in the package of heat X-Tool Metal Fab laser welder. Loosen the screw a bit.

286
00:25:13,680 --> 00:25:18,720
Slowly pull up the U-shaped component until its bottom reaches plus one. Tighten the screw.

287
00:25:19,600 --> 00:25:24,640
Pull the component back and forth to test if it's secured. Install the cutting tip back to

288
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:32,080
the welding head. Close the fastener. Reinstall the welding head on the carriage and ensure that

289
00:25:32,080 --> 00:25:40,200
the cable is properly placed. Click OK after the laser focus calibration concludes. Calibration

290
00:25:40,200 --> 00:25:55,390
Task 3. Red Spot Calibration. Click Start. Read the tips in the dialog box. Click Next.

291
00:25:55,390 --> 00:26:03,130
Follow the tips in the dialog box. Peel off the laser alignment sticker. Attach the sticker to

292
00:26:03,130 --> 00:26:09,130
the laser module and mind the orientation. Close the lid. Click Single Light Emission.

293
00:26:10,170 --> 00:26:14,010
After the operation is done, open the lid and take out the sticker.

294
00:26:14,010 --> 00:26:16,970
Check if the spot falls in the center of the concentric circles.

295
00:26:19,050 --> 00:26:22,330
You may use the clear tape instead following the same steps.

296
00:26:23,930 --> 00:26:27,850
If the spot deviates from the center of the concentric circles as shown,

297
00:26:28,570 --> 00:26:34,250
click Not Centered. Follow the tips to test the red spot position. Open the fastener.

298
00:26:34,250 --> 00:26:40,890
Turn the knob until it reaches negative 10, then close the fastener. Press the red stamp

299
00:26:40,890 --> 00:26:46,490
pad against the cutting tip to leave colors on the tip. Then secure the laser alignment card

300
00:26:46,490 --> 00:26:55,600
right under the cutting tip. Click Confirm. The cutting tip is automatically lowered.

301
00:26:55,600 --> 00:27:01,200
If it fails to touch the card, manually open the fastener and slightly rotate the knob

302
00:27:01,200 --> 00:27:07,680
until the red mark is left on the card. Then slowly lift the cutting tip and close the fastener.

303
00:27:07,680 --> 00:27:17,290
Click Next. Follow the tips to adjust the red spot position. To adjust the red spot left or right,

304
00:27:17,290 --> 00:27:20,490
gently loosen or tighten the welding head screws with the hex key.

305
00:27:21,210 --> 00:27:26,170
To adjust the red spot forward or backward, click the corresponding button in XCS.

306
00:27:26,890 --> 00:27:32,250
When the red spot is centered, click Complete the adjustment. Click Done. Click Done after

307
00:27:32,330 --> 00:27:40,250
the red spot calibration concludes. Example project. Place a slat with its teeth facing up.

308
00:27:40,250 --> 00:27:43,930
Ensure that its ends fit snugly into two slots in the working area.

309
00:27:44,570 --> 00:27:51,520
Place slats at equal intervals as needed. Place a material on the slats. Rotate the

310
00:27:51,520 --> 00:27:57,440
right fixture knob counterclockwise. Insert the right side of the material into the right fixture.

311
00:27:57,440 --> 00:28:02,240
Rotate the knob clockwise to tighten the right fixture. Rotate the left fixture knob

312
00:28:02,240 --> 00:28:07,680
counterclockwise. Lift the linkage lever. Move the left fixture to the right to hold the material.

313
00:28:08,320 --> 00:28:12,560
Rotate the knob clockwise to tighten the left fixture. Lower the linkage lever.

314
00:28:13,520 --> 00:28:21,600
Open XCS and place the object on the material. Click the object. Click Unknown material at the

315
00:28:21,600 --> 00:28:27,760
upper right corner. Choose the corresponding material. Choose the corresponding tip.

316
00:28:31,040 --> 00:28:40,090
Click Calibrate the capacitive sensor. Click Process. Before processing,

317
00:28:40,090 --> 00:28:45,050
check whether the requirements listed on the right panel are met. If yes, click Start.

318
00:28:48,220 --> 00:28:54,080
Click Continue processing. Press the Start slash Stop button.

319
00:28:57,560 --> 00:29:03,080
Wear your heat-resistant gloves and pull out the base plate. Enjoy your first product.
